<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canna</span></b> , ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάννα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a reed</i>, <i>cane</i> (less
			freq. than harundo), <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 9, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 32, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palustris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 298</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tremulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 6, 326</span></i>
			 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>any thing made of
				reed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A reed-pipe</i>, <i>flute</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				682</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 171</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 7,
			439</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A small vessel</i>, <i>gondola</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
				89</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 2, 2, § 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 56</span></i>. 57, §
			206.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> Canna
			gutturis. in later medical writers, <i>the
			windpipe</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Acut. 2, 16, 97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Tard. 2, 12, 137</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
